BT /F1 9 Tf 54 760 Td 12 TL (TIPS: Treasury Inflation-Protected Securities) Tj T* () Tj T* (FinTekkers knowledge library. Written in our own words from the Treasury's) Tj T* (published rules; the primary sources are listed at the end. A TIPS pays a) Tj T* (fixed real coupon on a principal that is adjusted for inflation by the CPI.) Tj T* () Tj T* (1 Scope {#scope}) Tj T* () Tj T* (How the index ratio, the inflation-adjusted principal, coupons, price and) Tj T* (accrued interest of a TIPS are formed, what happens when the CPI is late or) Tj T* (changes, and the deflation floor at maturity.) Tj T* () Tj T* (2 Reference CPI {#reference-cpi}) Tj T* () Tj T* (The index is the non-seasonally adjusted CPI-U published by the Bureau of) Tj T* (Labor Statistics. The reference CPI \(Ref CPI\) for the first day of a month M) Tj T* (is the CPI-U for the month three months earlier: for 1 July it is the April) Tj T* (CPI-U. For any other day of month M it is interpolated in a straight line) Tj T* (between the Ref CPI of the first of M and the first of the next month:) Tj T* () Tj T* (    Ref CPI\(date\) = Ref CPI\(M\) + \(t - 1\) / D * \(Ref CPI\(M+1\) - Ref CPI\(M\)\)) Tj T* () Tj T* (where t is the day of the month of the date and D is the number of days in) Tj T* (month M. The regulation fixes the rounding: the result is truncated to six) Tj T* (decimal places and rounded to five.) Tj T* () Tj T* (3 Index ratio {#index-ratio}) Tj T* () Tj T* (The index ratio on a date is the Ref CPI on that date divided by the Ref CPI) Tj T* (on the security's dated date \(its base CPI, published with the auction\):) Tj T* () Tj T* (    Index ratio\(date\) = Ref CPI\(date\) / Ref CPI\(dated date\)) Tj T* () Tj T* (It is also truncated to six decimals and rounded to five. On settlement the) Tj T* (ratio is taken at the settlement date.) Tj T* () Tj T* (4 Adjusted principal, coupon, price and accrued {#adjusted-principal}) Tj T* () Tj T* (- Inflation-adjusted principal = par * index ratio.) Tj T* (- Each coupon = \(real coupon rate / 2\) * inflation-adjusted principal on the) Tj T* (  coupon date.) Tj T* (- Prices and yields are quoted in real terms. The settlement amount per 100) Tj T* (  is \(real clean price + real accrued interest\) * index ratio at settlement.) Tj T* (- Real accrued interest is computed as for any Treasury note, on ACT/ACT) Tj T* (  ICMA \(see the day-count document\), then scaled by the index ratio.) Tj T* () Tj T* (5 Deflation floor {#deflation-floor}) Tj T* () Tj T* (At maturity the holder receives the greater of the inflation-adjusted) Tj T* (principal and the original par. Coupons are not floored: in a deflationary) Tj T* (period they are paid on the lower adjusted principal. The floor applies only) Tj T* (once, at maturity, so it is an option on cumulative inflation since issue.) Tj T* () Tj T* (6 Fallback index {#fallback-index}) Tj T* () Tj T* (If the CPI-U for a month is not reported when it is needed, Treasury uses a) Tj T* (substitute built from the last reported CPI-U and the change over the last) Tj T* (twelve months:) Tj T* ET
