BT /F1 9 Tf 54 760 Td 12 TL () Tj T* (    CPI\(missing\) = CPI\(last\) * \(CPI\(last\) / CPI\(last, 12 months earlier\)\)^\(m / 12\)) Tj T* () Tj T* (where m is the number of months between the last reported month and the) Tj T* (missing month. Payments made on a substitute index are not revised when the) Tj T* (real index is published. If the CPI is rebased, Treasury converts it back to) Tj T* (the original base; if it is discontinued or fundamentally changed, Treasury,) Tj T* (after consulting the Bureau of Labor Statistics, chooses an appropriate) Tj T* (replacement index.) Tj T* () Tj T* (7 Real yield {#real-yield}) Tj T* () Tj T* (The real yield is solved from the real clean price plus real accrued, with) Tj T* (the fixed-coupon formula in the bond maths document. The index ratio scales) Tj T* (both sides of the price equation, so it does not change the real yield.) Tj T* () Tj T* (8 Worked example {#tips-example}) Tj T* () Tj T* (An illustrative calculation with made-up CPI values. Ref CPI for 1 July is) Tj T* (300.00000 and for 1 August is 301.24000; July has 31 days; the base CPI is) Tj T* (295.00000. Settlement on 15 July:) Tj T* () Tj T* (- Ref CPI = 300.00000 + 14/31 * 1.24000 = 300.56000.) Tj T* (- Index ratio = 300.56000 / 295.00000 = 1.01885 \(five decimals\).) Tj T* (- A real clean price of 99.50 with real accrued 0.40 settles at) Tj T* (  \(99.50 + 0.40\) * 1.01885 = 101.7831 per 100 face.) Tj T* () Tj T* (Sources) Tj T* () Tj T* (- US Treasury, 31 CFR Part 356, Appendix B, section I \(inflation-protected) Tj T* (  securities: Ref CPI, index ratio, substitute index and the minimum) Tj T* (  principal at maturity\):) Tj T* (  https://www.ecfr.gov/current/title-31/subtitle-B/chapter-II/subchapter-A/part-356) Tj T* (- TreasuryDirect, Treasury Inflation-Protected Securities:) Tj T* (  https://www.treasurydirect.gov/marketable-securities/tips/) Tj T* (- US Bureau of Labor Statistics, Consumer Price Index \(CPI-U, not) Tj T* (  seasonally adjusted\): https://www.bls.gov/cpi/) Tj T* ET
